<section background-overlay="tint" background-overlay-intensity="0.38" vertical-align="center">
  <ai-image background="true" aspect-ratio="landscape" image-style="celestial-copperplate" prompt="Digitally illustrated copperplate celestial engraving of a brass telescope aimed across a vast deep-space field, precise ivory coordinate arcs widening across an abyssal-blue sky, cyan spectral traces and one restrained coral signal, a tiny generic ship silhouette low at the far right for scale, generous dark negative space on the left, no central explosion, no text or lettering"></ai-image>
  <grid spacing="none">
    <grid-item>
      <p role="eyebrow">No shore, no center</p>
      <h1 font-size="52pt" style="padding-right: 34%">Captain, reverse the telescope</h1>
      <p font-size="lg" style="padding-right: 42%"><b>Across distant galaxies, one clue repeats:</b> the universe is not debris racing from a blast point. Space itself has been stretching for about 13.8 billion years.</p>
      <spacer mode="fixed" size="24pt"></spacer>
      <hr horizontalAlign="left" width="xs" thickness="md" color="accent"/>
      <p font-size="sm">Our course follows three bearings · Expansion · Cooling · Evidence</p>
    </grid-item>
  </grid>
</section>